## 3. Agentic Capabilities (Generated Code)

### Built-in Tools Required
All generated agents must have access to the following tools:

#### File Operations
- `file-read` - Read file contents
- `file-write` - Write/append to files
- `file-search` - Search file names (glob patterns)
- `file-move` - Move/rename files
- `file-delete` - Delete files
- `grep` - Search file contents with regex

#### Web Capabilities
- `web-fetch` - Fetch web pages
- `web-scrape` - Extract structured data from HTML
- `web-search` - Search web via APIs

#### Shell Operations
- `shell-exec` - Execute shell commands with timeout
- `shell-safe` - Sanitized command execution

#### Utility
- `memory-save` - Save conversation context
- `memory-load` - Load conversation context
- `log-write` - Write structured logs

### Agentic Features
- Multi-step workflows (sequences of steps)
- Parallel execution capability
- Tool calling
- Stateful conversations
- Async execution (tokio runtime)
- Memory management (sliding window with configurable backends)
- **Looping with validation criteria** - Loops that continue until conditions are met
- **Multi-agent spawning and aggregation** - Spawn multiple local agents and aggregate results

### Tool Permissions (Multi-Level)
- **Agent-level permissions** - Permissions granted to entire agent (all tools)
- **Step-level permissions** - Permissions for specific workflow step
- **Tool-level permissions** - Fine-grained permission per individual tool
- **Permission inheritance** - Child steps inherit parent permissions unless explicitly overridden
- **Permission restrictions** - Ability to deny specific tools while allowing others

### Loop Control and Termination

#### Loop Types
- **Count-based loops** - Execute N times then terminate
- **Time-based loops** - Execute for specified duration
- **Validation-based loops** - Continue until validation criteria is met
- **Convergence loops** - Continue until results stabilize (delta < threshold)
- **Infinite loops** - Continue until explicit termination

#### Termination Conditions
- **Success conditions** - Loop exits when desired outcome achieved
- **Failure conditions** - Loop exits on error or failed validation
- **Timeout conditions** - Loop exits after maximum time elapsed
- **Convergence conditions** - Loop exits when changes between iterations fall below threshold
- **Manual conditions** - Loop continues until explicitly stopped

#### Expected Timespans
- **Fast operations** (<1 second): File reads, simple calculations
- **Medium operations** (1-10 seconds): File writes, web fetches, grep searches
- **Slow operations** (10-60 seconds): Large file processing, web scraping
- **Very slow operations** (60+ seconds): Model training, large analysis tasks
- **User-configurable timeouts** - Each operation type allows custom timeout override

