### 21.5 Multi-Instance Model Control

**Requirement**: Generate code that supports loading multiple model instances simultaneously.

**Why Needed**:
- Use cases: Mix different models, parallel inference, A/B testing
- Llama.cpp supports multiple instances via separate structs
- Users need to switch between models at runtime

**Transpiler Responsibilities**:
1. Parse multi-instance configuration from YAML
2. Generate a ModelManager struct with HashMap storage
3. Provide methods for model selection and switching
4. Ensure thread-safe access (Arc<RwLock>)

**Generated Code Pattern**:
```rust
use std::collections::HashMap;
use std::sync::Arc;
use tokio::sync::RwLock;

struct ModelManager {
    models: Arc<RwLock<HashMap<String, LlamaCppModelProvider>>>,
}

impl ModelManager {
    pub async fn get_model(&self, name: &str) -> Result<LlamaCppModelProvider> {
        let models = self.models.read().await;
        models.get(name)
            .cloned()
            .ok_or_else(|| ModelNotFound(name.to_string()))
    }

    pub async fn load_model(&mut self, name: &str, config: ModelConfig)
        -> Result<()> {
        let provider = LlamaCppModelProvider::new(config).await?;
        let mut models = self.models.write().await;
        models.insert(name.to_string(), provider);
        Ok(())
    }
}

// Usage in generated workflow
